    "narrative": "For Ghost Ride the WHIP on this May 21st, the priority is clear: capitalize on the exploitable matchup against Agnos. **Corbin Carroll** leads the squad with an elite 85.94 score, benefiting from a massive 19% SP skill bump and his advantageous slot at the top of the lineup. He is our primary engine for the scarce SB category today. Similarly, **Gabriel Moreno** benefits from that same soft pitching profile, climbing to a 65.25 rating. While **James Wood** finds himself hitting against a tougher southpaw in Peterson, his 62.77 score remains strong due to his leadoff positioning, which provides the necessary volume to outweigh the moderate pitching skill.\n\nThe rest of the lineup hovers in a critical transition zone. **Kyle Karros** is our most efficient depth play at 59.92, bolstered by a 13% SP skill bump against Rodriguez. **Tyler Soderstrom** (56.73) and **Austin Riley** (55.56) are marginal starts; **Austin Riley** in particular was hampered by a negative BvP adjustment, though his efficiency in stolen base situations\u2014despite his profile\u2014kept him above the benching threshold. **Travis Bazzana** rounds out the starters at 49.78. With **Jose Caballero** and **Trevor Story** sidelined on the IL, and **Josh Naylor** and **Mickey Moniak** unavailable, our bench depth is currently limited to non-active players like **Brice Turang**, **Seiya Suzuki**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Max Muncy**, **Carson Williams**, **Zach McKinstry**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Alex Freeland**, **Cole Young**, and **Henry Bolte**, none of whom were viable pivots given the schedule. We are banking on **Corbin Carroll** to provide the high-end ceiling required to offset the moderate output expected from our infield pivots today.",
